R935: MAME 0.289's i960 with the chip's register ring modelled BESIDE its own
rule (Sega Model 2 core for MiSTer FPGA, study R935). R935_RING=<n> keeps the n
newest saved frames as the chip / the core's RING build do (a frame's save
area written only when a call finds the ring full, read back only when a return
finds it empty, flushreg writes all) and logs every program load or store that
touches a save area the modelled ring still holds -- where the core's RING
build would read or write memory MAME has already made current. MAME's own
execution is unchanged. R935_OUT=<file>: FIRST lines as they happen, totals
and per-PC counts at exit. What it showed: The House of the Dead, 75 s of play
through the courtyard, ring 8 and ring 4: 1,856,215 calls, 14,283 flushreg,
0 hazards.
Apply after sim/io/mame_i960_formlog.patch: patch -p1 < mame_i960_ring.patch,
then make SUBTARGET=m2lod SOURCES=src/mame/sega/model2.cpp. MAME code
(BSD-3-Clause, i960.cpp's own licence); a tool, not part of the core.

